PTX LB-self+alias+acquire+weak-store
"One thread loads global x through its alias y with ld.acquire, then stores 1 to x with st.release and 2 with a weak store; the load reads 2. A release pattern ends with a strong write (8.8), so the release store followed by the weak store is not one that the load could observe, and nothing synchronizes; with no alias fence nothing orders the load before the stores to the alias (8.6): allowed."
{
x=0;
y @ generic aliases x;
P0:r0=0;
}
 P0@cta 0,gpu 0              ;
 ld.acquire.gpu r0, y        ;
 st.release.gpu x, 1         ;
 st.weak x, 2                ;
exists
(P0:r0 == 2 /\ x == 2)
